# Dockerfile.dockerignore — BuildKit per-Dockerfile ignore for
# benches/latency/ros2/docker/Dockerfile (whose build context is the
# REPO ROOT — its COPY paths are repo-root-relative).
#
# BuildKit picks this file up because it sits next to the Dockerfile
# and is named <Dockerfile>.dockerignore; the legacy (non-BuildKit)
# builder IGNORES it and would tar the full repo — .git and target/
# included, tens of GB — into the context. The canonical build path
# (bench.py::ensure_docker_image) therefore sets DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1 on
# the `docker build` child, so an engine without BuildKit refuses
# loudly instead of quietly uploading the repo root. A hand-run
# `docker build` must export it too (it is the default since Docker 23).
#
# Paths are relative to the CONTEXT ROOT (the repo root).
#
# BLOCKLIST, not allowlist, on purpose: the ignore file's job is to
# keep the heavy artifacts out of the context, not to enumerate what
# the image may see — an allowlist would silently break the build
# whenever the bench tree grows.

# VCS + build output (the heavy hitters).
.git
**/target

# Archives / recordings / result artifacts that may sit in a working
# tree (never needed to compile the bench packages).
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.mcap
**/__pycache__
benches/**/results
benches/**/raw

# Host-side colcon artifacts, if anyone ever builds the bench ws on
# the host (the image always colcon-builds its own copy).
benches/latency/ros2/ros2_ws
